  "id": "osf-review-container-only",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-08T14:12:10.513Z",
  "title": "Codex review runs container-only; reviewer homes kept for diagnosis",
  "summary": "This change removes the factory-container detection machinery and the pre-flight sandbox check from the reviewer path. Codex no longer has a read-only mode of its own: it always runs with `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`, because the review container is the wall. In exchange, the workflow now sets `OSF_KEEP_REVIEW_HOME=1` and points `TMPDIR` at a mounted `out/reviewer-home`, so each reviewer's home survives its run and is uploaded as a diagnostic artifact; a kept home has its seeded login files deleted first so no credential rides out with it.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
